          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Eugenia axillaris, the white stopper, is a species of flowering plant in the family Myrtaceae. It is native to central and southern Florida, the Caribbean, Bermuda, eastern Mexico, and Central America. An evergreen shrub or tree reaching {{cvt|20|to|30|ft|0}} but often shorter, it is typically found in partly shady coastal hammocks and other sandy areas."
